WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.899
National Treasure spoke to the hearts and
minds of many a young history enthusiast — and

00:00:04.899 --> 00:00:08.500
action thriller fans everywhere — when it
hit theaters in 2004.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.970
The box office smash featured Nicolas Cage
as Ben Gates, an explorer who steals the Declaration

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.600
of Independence in his quest to find a hidden
treasure.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.990
A sequel, National Treasure: Book of Secrets,
was released in 2007 and improved on the first

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.450
film's box office return.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:28.010
Talk about a third film started shortly after,
and although rumors have persisted over the

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.170
years, nothing has come of those stories.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:35.270
Unfortunately for fans of the franchise, production
appears to have stalled on the third film.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:41.190
Here's why it's unlikely that Disney will
ever actually release National Treasure 3.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.699
Busy producer

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:47.629
Famed producer Jerry Bruckheimer is the man
behind many of your favorite action movie

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:51.269
franchises, including Beverly Hills Cop, Bad
Boys, and Pirates of the Caribbean.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:55.690
Jerry Bruckheimer Films was also one of the
production companies that worked on the National

00:00:55.690 --> 00:01:00.100
Treasure series, but that might be what's
holding up a potential third film.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.070
Bruckheimer has said that he's still looking
to, quote, "get this thing going" in reference

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:08.250
to the third film, but right now his plate
is pretty full with his work on long-awaited

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.370
sequels for some of his other popular franchises.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:15.890
These films include Bad Boys for Life, a third
installment in the Bad Boys series.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:21.190
He's also working on a Tom Cruise-led Top
Gun sequel, titled Top Gun: Maverick, which

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.530
is slated for a 2019 release.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.640
With so many other movies awaiting his attention,
Bruckheimer likely doesn't have much time

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.830
to devote to National Treasure 3.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:31.830
Fact-checking

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.790
The National Treasure films may not be the
most historically accurate to ever grace the

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:37.790
big screen...

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:38.870
"Let me guess!

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.500
It's the wrong time!

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.120
It's the wrong place!

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.350
I'm wrong again!"

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.420
… but apparently quite a lot of research
still goes into making them, and that could

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.850
be part of what's delayed National Treasure
3 for so long.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:56.310
As Cage revealed in 2016, it's been a challenge
getting the script "where it needs to be"

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.550
thanks to the unique constraints of the franchise.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:01:59.780
He told Entertainment Weekly,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.790
"I do know that those scripts are very difficult
to write, because there has to be some credibility

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:09.579
in terms of the facts and fact-checking, because
it was relying on historical events.

00:02:09.579 --> 00:02:11.480
And then you have to make it entertaining."

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.613
"There's thousands of years of world history
down there.

00:02:13.613 --> 00:02:16.930
And it belongs to the world."

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:21.530
Jon Turteltaub, who directed both films and
is attached to the third, also said script

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.709
issues have been plaguing the film, telling
Collider in 2013,

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:29.420
"[It's] so damn hard to write a great historical
mystery based on fact."

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.319
Turtletaub said at the time that he thought
they'd be shooting the film within two years,

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:39.200
but it appears that getting the script just
right has been a longer process than he anticipated.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.129
Critical aversion

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:44.959
Critical success isn't always tied to box
office success, and the National Treasure

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:48.219
franchise is a perfect example of that principle
in action.

00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:53.269
The franchise has even earned a number of
nominations at the Golden Raspberry Awards,

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:57.999
honoring the worst Hollywood has to offer,
including a Worst Actor nod for Cage for Book

00:02:57.999 --> 00:02:58.999
of Secrets.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.000
"I'm wrong again!

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:01.720
Wrong about us.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.280
Wrong about Thomas Gates.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.340
Wrong as you'd like, the Queen Anne chair."

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.239
The fact that critics were never on board
with the franchise could be something that

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:13.049
has deterred the studio from ordering another
movie.

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:17.730
The falling critical and box office returns
of other franchises like Transformers and

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:22.739
Pirates of the Caribbean hint that reviews
do matter, and making another film in a franchise

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:26.749
that's already earned critics' ire could be
too great a risk.

00:03:26.749 --> 00:03:28.849
Cage's decline

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:33.239
The National Treasure franchise managed to
improve its grosses from the first film to

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:37.920
the second, but Nicolas Cage has been seeing
his box office returns fall for quite some

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:38.640
time now.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:50.200
Aside from his Ghost Rider franchise, Kick-Ass,
and his voice role in The Croods, Cage has

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.430
led a series of commercial flops in recent
years, which could make the studio reluctant

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.739
to rely on him as a leading man once again.

00:03:56.739 --> 00:04:00.959
Cage has reportedly been taking roles "left
and right" the past decade to help him pay

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:04.829
off his debts, which could explain his string
of smaller films.

00:04:04.829 --> 00:04:08.809
Financial need may be enough to get him back
to the franchise, but the studio could be

00:04:08.809 --> 00:04:12.019
leery of signing a star whose box office appeal
is in question.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.380
"I'm like a prickly pear!"

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.860
Disney's priorities

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.660
A lot has changed for Disney since Book of
Secrets hit theaters in 2007.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.420
While the studio was never a minor player
in the movie marketplace, their influence

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:30.060
has been stepped up significantly in the past
few years, mostly thanks to major moves in

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.030
picking up Marvel and Lucasfilm.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:36.720
Since the last National Treasure was released,
Disney gained a lot more franchises to work

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.480
with, and they're not slowing down.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:42.970
They don't need to go back to a franchise
that's been in limbo for a decade.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.350
Changing landscape

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:48.540
A solid franchise used to be a guarantee that
audiences would turn out for a movie, but

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.530
the box office has changed a lot in recent
years.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:55.510
Recent franchises that have seen diminishing
returns at the box office include Bruckheimer's

00:04:55.510 --> 00:05:00.540
Pirates of the Caribbean movies, the Transformers
franchise, Tom Cruise's The Mummy and Dwayne

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.160
Johnson's Baywatch.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.410
While there are a few high-profile exceptions,
including Marvel's continued box office dominance,

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:11.620
it's risky to assume National Treasure would
be one of them, which could be just one more

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.200
reason Disney won't release National Treasure
3.

